{"tool_name":"macrel","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"macrel","identifiers":["doi:10.1101/2019.12.17.880385"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A pipeline for AMP (antimicrobial peptide) prediction","home_url":"https://github.com/BigDataBiology/macrel","keywords":["Genomics","Peptides","Metagenomics","Metagenome"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":12},"biotools":{"id":"macrel","home":"https://big-data-biology.org/software/macrel","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Antimicrobial peptide screening in genomes and metagenomes.\n\nMacrel: (Meta)genomic AMP Classification and Retrieval.\n\nPipeline to mine antimicrobial peptides (AMPs) from (meta)genomes.","addition_date":"2021-03-19T08:28:04Z","last_update_date":"2021-04-11T09:02:40Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library","Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:macrel","credit":[{"email":"luis@luispedro.org","name":"Luis Pedro Coelho","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9280-7885","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Data retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2422"},{"term":"Homology-based gene prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3663"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"name":"Macrel","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.7717/PEERJ.10555","metadata":{"abstract":"Copyright 2020 Santos-J\u00fanior et al.Motivation: Antimicrobial peptides (AMPs) have the potential to tackle multidrug-resistant pathogens in both clinical and non-clinical contexts. The recent growth in the availability of genomes and metagenomes provides an opportunity for in silico prediction of novel AMP molecules. However, due to the small size of these peptides, standard gene prospection methods cannot be applied in this domain and alternative approaches are necessary. In particular, standard gene prediction methods have low precision for short peptides, and functional classification by homology results in low recall. Results: Here, we present Macrel (for metagenomic AMP classification and retrieval), which is an end-to-end pipeline for the prospection of high-quality AMP candidates from (meta)genomes. For this, we introduce a novel set of 22 peptide features. These were used to build classifiers which perform similarly to the state-of-the-art in the prediction of both antimicrobial and hemolytic activity of peptides, but with enhanced precision (using standard benchmarks as well as a stricter testing regime). We demonstrate that Macrel recovers high-quality AMP candidates using realistic simulations and real data.","authors":[{"name":"Coelho L.P."},{"name":"Pan S."},{"name":"Santos-Junior C.D."},{"name":"Zhao X.-M."}],"citationCount":1,"date":"2020-12-18T00:00:00Z","journal":"PeerJ","title":"Macrel: Antimicrobial peptide screening in genomes and metagenomes"},"pmcid":"PMC7751412","pmid":"33384902"}],"topic":[{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Metagenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3174"},{"term":"Microbial ecology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3697"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"Macrel","home":"https://bio.tools/macrel","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Antimicrobial peptide screening in genomes and metagenomes.\n\nMacrel: (Meta)genomic AMP Classification and Retrieval.\n\nPipeline to mine antimicrobial peptides (AMPs) from (meta)genomes.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:macrel/cmd/big-data-biology.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false,"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment